Description:
    Adds "Sign in with Mixin" to this Rails application using OmniAuth
    (omniauth-mixin): User/Session/Current models, a sessions controller with
    the OAuth callback, an authentication concern, routes, migrations, and
    the OmniAuth initializer.

    The generated login is identity-only: the OAuth access token is used to
    establish identity and is not persisted.

    After generating, set MIXIN_CLIENT_ID and MIXIN_CLIENT_SECRET, and register
    https://<your-host>/auth/mixin/callback as the OAuth redirect URL in the
    Mixin developer dashboard.

Example:
    rails generate mixin_bot:authentication

    This will create:
        config/initializers/omniauth.rb
        app/models/user.rb
        app/models/session.rb
        app/models/current.rb
        app/controllers/sessions_controller.rb
        app/controllers/concerns/authentication.rb
        app/views/sessions/new.html.erb
        db/migrate/xxx_create_users.rb
        db/migrate/xxx_create_sessions.rb

    It will also add `omniauth-mixin` and `omniauth-rails_csrf_protection` to
    the Gemfile and inject `include Authentication` into ApplicationController.
